    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and the build is green.\n\nDone. The change adds `ownerSegment` to the owner API response.\n\n**What I did** \u2014 kept structural impact minimal by adding behaviour as a new cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method/class:\n\n1. **New class `OwnerSegment`** (`rest/function/owner/OwnerSegment.java`) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper mirroring the existing `OwnerLocality`/`OwnerMembershipLevel` style. `of(owner)` returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`: TIER is `PREMIUM` at effective membership level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when `OwnerLocality.region(owner)` is NSW/VIC/QLD else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the two existing derivations, so it has near-zero surrounding complexity.\n2. **One `@Mapping` line** in `OwnerMapper` wiring `ownerSegment` to `OwnerSegment.of(owner)` \u2014 same pattern as the other derived read-only fields.\n3. **`ownerSegment` field** in `openapi.yml` (read-only), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\nThe tier uses the effective membership level (`owner.getMembershipLevel()` with fallback to `OwnerMembershipLevel.of(owner)`), consistent with how the mapper already exposes `membershipLevel`. Both acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for Sydney/NSW, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) and the full suite pass.",
